R&C patch 7054: per-await log (diagnostic, off by default) and GPU-fetch pipelines in the exported template
(load stalls, the RE notes s.30).
1. LD_PSO_AWAIT_LOG=1 prints one [pso-await] line per build the walker waits on: frame, key, src (M = a miss the
   lookahead never submitted, A = a lookahead submission, P = an earlier walker submission), state when the wait began
   (q = queued, r = running or finished, not merged), wait, age (submission to the wait), queue length, in-flight, the
   walker's END count and the last scan's END count, horizon and stop reason. It attributes each post-load gap to its
   pipelines (the static reading of prio-on-cold could only count them). PSO entries keep their submission time.
2. Template export (KZ3 2071 LD_PSO_TEMPLATE_OUT): 2076 skipped GPU-fetch draws, expecting their packed record, which
   the walker never builds with LD_VTX_GPU=1 (R&C's default), so a ToD template would have held no GPU-fetch pipeline
   (the 7051 bug, in the template). A GPU-fetch draw now notes its packed record (key from the same key head with
   packed mode 1, vgpu off); the prewarm derives the GPU-fetch variant as 2076 intended and rejects a record whose key
   does not reproduce ([pso-tmpl] failed_key), which the template A/B checks.
No host test: (1) is a log line; (2) needs the walker's translator and key tail (Windows build), checked by the
prewarm's own key check in the run.

